comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T18:29:05.782Z",codex-agent,"Native SDK tests: 25 concurrency and interruption cases passed. Competing writes injected at all six mutation boundaries; exact duplicate requests converge to one audit event; stale requests refuse without a write and succeed only after an explicit reread. Two OS writers acknowledged and retained twelve distinct observations; hard exits before and after commit converged on the original key. Source and transport gates remain in progress."
  "2026-11-06T19:11:16.517Z",codex-agent,"Native single-owner CAS and create-if-absent preserve immutable operation receipts, outcome evidence and peer fields. Linked concurrency/capacity run passes 30 tests, including every instrumented competing-write boundary, same-key replay, independent OS writers and hard process interruption. Prior complete 500-sequence model run passed with 156 observations and 228 acknowledged domain mutations; the final model also checks native related edges on every read-back. Behavioral reverts independently fail the tuple-membership, changed-replay, stale-CAS and mutation-budget checks; each restored behavior passes. Four red and four restored green proofs, all in disposable copies."
  "2026-11-06T21:07:47.162Z",codex-agent,"Independent review identified a candidate receipt-integrity edge: equal receipt and outcome counts plus receipt-to-outcome existence do not establish a one-to-one binding. Reproduce with two real native observations and a duplicated result identity in a scratch tracker. Require invalid_record if confirmed; preserve native audit history and add a behavioral revert proof."
  "2026-11-06T21:10:45.512Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed and fixed a malformed stored-state acceptance: two record receipts could bind the same execution while another outcome had no receipt. Native SDK regression first failed with Missing expected rejection; requiring unique recorded result identities now refuses both owner reads and coverage as invalid_record, without a new history event. The linked focused test passes 1 of 1. Five isolated behavioral reverts now fail as intended and all five restored versions pass. This is an independent finding, not a CodeRabbit thread."
  "2026-11-08T10:24:06.605Z",codex-agent,"Review fixes preserve explicit retry semantics while retrying both lock_conflict and revision_conflict after rereading state. Deterministic helper tests inject both contention codes and verify unrelated refusals propagate; independent OS writers retain all twelve acknowledged outcomes. Native missing-item, missing-required-option and missing-related-target assertions now require their exact codes. Three wrong-code injections fail the strengthened tests and pass after restoration. Every linked storage/kernel/proof command now builds first; all four clean-dist command probes fail when their build prefix is removed and pass with it. No audit history was rewritten."
